From simon.urbanek at r-project.org  Thu Apr 28 19:24:44 2011
From: simon.urbanek at r-project.org (Simon Urbanek)
Date: Thu, 28 Apr 2011 15:24:44 -0400
Subject: Re: plotting question
In-Reply-To: <BANLkTimakaANj0sF+=d37DVjjUx3s3A2XQ@mail.gmail.com>
References: <BANLkTimakaANj0sF+=d37DVjjUx3s3A2XQ@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <6E653C82-BA3B-43D3-BE4A-C91F85467FE3@r-project.org>

You can't use Quartz in Rserve (default in png() is to use Quartz) because Apple doesn't support CF calls in forked programs, so the easiest way is to use Cairo package for graphics output (see, for example FastRWeb). So you add library(Cairo) and replace png with CairoPNG.

Cheers,
Simon


